arty":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Matters of Urgency - Climate Change - Climate Change Summit and emissions reduction target","noes":33,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2014-09-22.148.1) moved by Greens Senator [Christine Milne](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/members/senate/tasmania/christine_milne), which was: _That, in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a [matter of urgency](http://www.aph.gov.au/About_Parliament/Senate/Powers_practice_n_procedures/Brief_Guides_to_Senate_Procedure/No_9):_ _\"The need for the [Prime minister](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/members/representatives/warringah/tony_abbott) to attend the [United Nations Climate Summit 2014](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_Summit),(Read more about the UN Climate Summit 2014 on its website [here](http://www.un.org/climatechange/summit/). ) and to recognise that [Australia's emissions reduction target](http://www.climatechange.gov.au/climate-change/greenhouse-gas-measurement-and-reporting/australias-emissions-projections/australias) is inadequate.\"_ This means that the majority disagree with this motion and that it was rejected. _Background to the motion_ The [2014 Climate Change Summit](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_Summit) was announced by UN Secretary-General [Ban Ki-moon](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ban_Ki-moon) in 2013 and takes place on 23 September 2014 in New York. It is a meeting on [climate change](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change) with a focus on initiatives and actions. Secretary-General Ban invited leaders of governments, the private sector and civil society with the aim of these leaders using the Summit as a public platform.(Read more about the Summit on its website [here](http://www.un.org/climatechange/summit/about/).)","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3427","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2014-09-22/3"}
